      "content": "Subject: Your Application for Software Engineer Position\n\nDear [Candidate's Name],\n\nI hope this message finds you in good spirits. I wanted to personally reach out to you after our recent interview process for the Software Engineer position at [Company Name]. We truly enjoyed getting to know you and discussing your impressive background and passion for software engineering.\n\nWe were genuinely impressed with your skills and experience, and it was a pleasure to learn more about your journey. However, after careful consideration, we have decided to move forward with another candidate whose qualifications closely align with our current needs.\n\nPlease know that this decision was not easy, and we genuinely appreciate the opportunity to have considered you for this role. We were particularly impressed by your dedication and passion for software engineering, and we hope you will keep our door open for future opportunities.\n\nWe wish you the best of luck in your job search and future endeavors. If you have any questions or need further assistance, please don't hesitate to reach out.\n\nWarm regards,\n\n[Your Name]\n[Your Position]\n[Company Name]\n\nP.S. We hope you don't mind the little \"goblin\" reference in our company culture. We always appreciate a good laugh and a friendly rivalry!",
